<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U gets British ok for glaucoma drug.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U gets British ok for glaucoma drug.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish-U.S. drug company Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said on Friday its Xalatan glaucoma drug had won approval from British authorities.  </p>
<p>&quot;This approval is an important step for Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn when it comes to the process of making Xalatan available all over Europe. We expect to have Xalatan approved in ither EU countries in the middle of 1997,&quot; said Goran Ando, Executive Vice-President, World-wide Science and Technology for P&amp;U.</p>
<p>P&amp;U said the indication approved was of elevated intraocular pressure in patients with open angle glaucoma and ocular hypertension who are intolerant to other medication.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
